- final-commit: pending-this-commit
- timestamp: 2026-04-29
- pr: pending
- summary: |
    HLAvariantRecord composite codec implemented per IEEE 1516.2-2010 §4.
    Discriminator value selects the alternative codec at runtime; padding
    between discriminator and selected alternative is computed from start
    of record to the alternative's OctetBoundary. Record-level
    OctetBoundary = max(disc, max alt) so nesting carries worst-case
    alignment outward. Unknown-discriminator paths on Encode and Decode
    return ErrEncTypeMismatch wrapped with context.
    4 new variant-record vectors land in tests/conformance/encoding_vectors.json
    in the contiguous TASK-016 / TASK-017 records block, exercising both
    {HLAoctet, HLAfloat64BE} and {HLAoctet, HLAinteger32BE} alternative sets
    and three distinct padding shapes (no pad, 4-byte pad, octet alt).
    Coverage on rti/pkg/encoding/variant_record.go: ~93% (>= 80%).
- acceptance:
    - 4 variant-record vectors covering different discriminator branches
    - explicit byte-layout assertions (not round-trip-only)
    - unknown-discriminator -> errors.Is(err, ErrEncTypeMismatch)
    - golangci-lint clean on rti/pkg/encoding
    - additive-only on encoding_vectors.json
